  nonce: 5fe5  # 5fe5
  data:  # 5fe5
    kind: work_item  # 5fe5
    title: "check-docstring-drift: add a registry-cross-reference sub-check (blame cannot find retired-vocabulary drift)"  # 5fe5
    status: todo_hard  # 5fe5
    priority: 2  # 5fe5
    parent:  # 5fe5
    tags:  # 5fe5
    - docs  # 5fe5
    - analysis_quality  # 5fe5
    isbefore: []  # 5fe5
    duplicate_of: []  # 5fe5
    not_duplicate_of: []  # 5fe5
    pr_ref:  # 5fe5
    description: "The docstring-drift scan has three sub-checks (co-change blame, tracker-ID\ncross-ref, phase-marker grep). None can find a docstring that names a\nRETIRED edge type or symbol kind, because none of them looks at the\nvocabulary registries.\n\nEVIDENCE (PR #414, dev @ 22418804f4). The co-change scan flagged 45 files.\nSemantic review found the dominant defect family was retired-vocabulary\nnames still documented as live. Verifying them by grepping each retired\nname repo-wide then found the SAME family in NINE MORE files that the scan\ndid not flag and structurally CANNOT flag -- their docstrings had not aged\nrelative to their bodies, so no blame-based signal exists:\n\n  route_handler.py      routes_to           -> dispatches_to  (4 sites)\n  framework_patterns.py routes_to           -> dispatches_to  (2 sites)\n  cli.py                routes_to           -> dispatches_to\n  ruby.py               invokes_callback    -> dispatches_to  (3 sites)\n  elixir.py             invokes_callback    -> dispatches_to\n  ipc.py                message_send/_receive -> event_publishes\n  phoenix_ipc.py        message_send/_receive -> event_publishes\n  controller_routes.py  contains_routes     -> contains\n  axis_meta_keys.py     message_publish/_subscribe -> event_publishes\n\nThe last one was NOT confined to a comment: axis_meta_keys.py's `topic`\nMetaKeySpec description feeds scripts/generate-schema, so the retired pair\nwas being PUBLISHED to JSON consumers in docs/schema.json. That is the\nsharpest argument for the check -- this defect class can escape the\ndocstring layer into a shipped artifact.\n\nPROPOSED CHECK (a fourth sub-check in scripts/check-docstring-drift).\nFor every .py under packages/*/src/, extract the module docstring and\ninline comments, and match identifier-shaped tokens against:\n  - the retired/absent set: names that look like an edge type or symbol\n    kind (snake_case, or kind=\"...\" literals) and are NOT in\n    edge_types.EDGE_TYPES / symbol_kinds registries.\nReport each hit with file:line and the token.\n\nWHY THIS SHAPE IS SAFE, unlike the sweep-skipper #410 refuted. It is\nname-EXACT and registry-derived: no blame heuristic, no date arithmetic,\nno threshold, so it cannot decay with the calendar the way the day-delta\narm did (28 -> 87 flags with nothing drifted). The registries are already\nthe single source of truth and are already CI-enforced for drift\n(check-edge-type-drift, check-symbol-kind-drift) -- this extends the same\nauthority to prose.\n\nKNOWN FALSE-POSITIVE SOURCE, and the answer. Docstrings legitimately name\nretired types while EXPLAINING the fold (\"the bespoke ``links_to`` type was\nfolded onto ``references``\"). Those must not flag. Two options, cheapest\nfirst: (a) suppress a hit whose line also matches /fold|retired|pre-fold|\ndeprecated|was .* onto|no longer/; (b) require an explicit allowlist\ncomment. Option (a) was sufficient by inspection over the ~12 such sites\nleft in-tree after PR #414 (compact.py:27, compact.py:137, ipc.py:12,\ncontroller_routes.py:51, router_routes.py:25, evidence_types.py, and the\ndocstrings PR #414 itself rewrote) -- but MEASURE the FP rate on the live\ntree before wiring it as a gate, and ship it advisory-only first.\n\nDO NOT wire this as a blocking gate on the first pass. Land it as a\nreported sub-check under --all, measure, then decide."  # 5fe5
    fields: {}  # 5fe5
- op: discuss  # 68ec
  at: '2026-08-19T05:39:40Z'  # 68ec
  by: agent  # 68ec
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 68ec
  clock: 2  # 68ec
  nonce: 68ec  # 68ec
  message: "POST-AUDIT RE-MEASUREMENT (dev @ 440b131d0a), and a SECOND known-limitation for the tracker-ref sub-check.\n\nCo-change flagged 45 -> 6 after PRs #414/#416. The clock-independent [commits] arm is at ZERO. All 6 survivors are true negatives: 4 were audited and came back 'matches' (extended1/__init__, lang-common/__init__, tracker/migration, tracker/sync_log), and the 2 NEWLY flagged ones I verified by hand -- linkers/ipc.py (flagged because a PR edited a FUNCTION docstring in it, moving the body while correctly leaving an accurate module docstring alone) and lang-common/rst.py (never audited; its claimed kinds section/directive/target and edges references/includes match the code exactly). So the instrument is at its floor, and every surviving flag is a file blame cannot tell is clean.\n\nTHE SECOND LIMITATION, which this item should handle. Tracker-refs went 30 -> 31. Five of the six 'new' hits are the same hits at shifted line numbers. The one genuinely new hit is lua.py:25 -- prose I wrote for #416:\n\n  'under INV-fahub a bare call that would resolve to a cross-table method by short name alone is deferred instead'\n\nINV-fahub is satisfied, and the check flags a closed ID whose context frames it as pending. But 'deferred' here describes what the CODE does to a call (defer_bare_method_call), not the status of the item. The heuristic cannot distinguish 'the tracker item is deferred' from 'the code defers this resolution', and the second is a normal way to write about a deferral mechanism. I deliberately did NOT reword it -- renaming the mechanism to dodge a lint would be worse documentation.\n\nLikely fix when this item is worked: require the pending-framing token to be ADJACENT to the ID rather than anywhere in the surrounding window. Same discipline as the proposed registry check: name-exact, no heuristic guessing.\n\n(Phase-markers 462 -> 465 is also an artifact -- all 15 changed hits are in base.py at shifted line numbers, because #416 added ~19 lines to its module docstring.)"  # 68ec
