  message: "OWNER RULING 2026-08-19, verbatim: 'yes, update the playbook. I approve and I approve using auto-pr without --gov'.\n\nScope: the docstring-staleness-audit playbook under .agent/agent_playbooks_protocols_sops_skills/. Approval covers editing it AND self-merging via auto-pr without the governance flag. Recorded here rather than left in conversation.\n\nContent going in: (1) calibration refreshed -- the documented 2026-05-15 figures (28 flagged / 21 real / 75%) are superseded by this run (45 flagged / 41 real / 91%) at the SAME thresholds; (2) two further measurement artifacts beyond the two documented -- the calendar-decay one #410 fixed, and the newly-observed 'a file re-flags when you edit a FUNCTION docstring inside it, because the scan's body region includes them' (this is what put linkers/ipc.py in the post-audit six); (3) the registry blind spot this item exists to close, so the next runner knows the scan cannot see retired-vocabulary drift; (4) the tracker-ref false-positive shapes, including the 'deferred' collision recorded above."  # af1e
- op: discuss  # fca9
  at: '2026-10-01T00:58:29Z'  # fca9
  by: agent  # fca9
  actor: jgstern_agent  # fca9
  clock: 4  # fca9
  nonce: fca9  # fca9
  message: "PREMISE CHECK 2026-09-30 (dev 7f0f993843): CURRENT-WITH-UPDATES. The fourth sub-check does not exist. The row's evidence sites were cleaned. Its proposed comparison set would misfire as written.\n- scripts/check-docstring-drift still has three sub-checks: --co-change, --tracker-refs, --phase-markers, and --all runs those three (docstring lines 11-61; --help printed the same). Its only commit since 08-19 is 433c90f9f1 (CI wiring). No registry cross-reference was added.\n- The nine filed live-use sites are gone. `grep -rnw` over packages/*/src finds routes_to 3, invokes_callback 1, contains_routes 2, message_publish/_subscribe 1 each. I read every one: each is fold-explanation prose (compact.py:27/137, route_handler.py:5, axis_meta_keys.py:423 \"folded from\", router_routes.py:25, controller_routes.py:51, message_queue.py:6). Those are exactly the lines the suppression regex in option (a) must pass.\n- CORRECTION 1: message_send / message_receive are not retired vocabulary. message_send is a LIVE evidence type (evidence_types.py:312, and :583 in the confidence table), and websocket.py:161 uses it in that sense. A check against only edge + symbol-kind registries would flag live evidence-type prose. The comparison set must include evidence_types.all_evidence_type_names(), and plausibly the io-boundary vocabulary too.\n- CORRECTION 2: edge_types.EDGE_TYPES is a tuple of EdgeTypeSpec, so `name in EDGE_TYPES` is always False (checked: 'contains' in EDGE_TYPES -> False). Use edge_types.all_edge_type_names() and symbol_kinds.all_symbol_kind_names().\n- The playbook records the blind spot and a manual stopgap (docstring-staleness-audit-playbook.md:88-106, \"Until WI-sipuk lands...\"), as discussion 2 planned.\n- NOT RUN: the scan itself (no FP-rate measurement). The tracker-refs \"adjacent token\" refinement from discussion 1 is also not implemented; I checked the script's argparse, not the lua.py hit.\nPROPOSED: amend the description's registry list (edge + symbol-kind + evidence-type, via the all_*_names() resolvers). Replace the nine-site evidence with \"cleaned by PR #414/#416; the class is unguarded\"."  # fca9
- op: update  # 4592
