  set:  # 4592
    description: "The docstring-drift scan (scripts/check-docstring-drift) has three sub-checks: --co-change\n(blame), --tracker-refs (tracker-ID cross-ref) and --phase-markers (grep); --all runs those\nthree. None can find a docstring that names a RETIRED edge type or symbol kind, because none\nof them looks at the vocabulary registries.\n\nEVIDENCE (PR #414, dev @ 22418804f4). The co-change scan flagged 45 files. Semantic review\nfound that the dominant defect family was retired-vocabulary names still documented as live.\nGrepping each retired name repo-wide then found the SAME family in NINE MORE files that the\nscan did not flag and structurally CANNOT flag: their docstrings had not aged relative to\ntheir bodies, so no blame-based signal existed. These were routes_to, invokes_callback,\ncontains_routes and message_publish/_subscribe across route_handler.py,\nframework_patterns.py, cli.py, ruby.py, elixir.py, ipc.py, phoenix_ipc.py,\ncontroller_routes.py and axis_meta_keys.py. One of them was NOT confined to a comment:\naxis_meta_keys.py's `topic` MetaKeySpec description feeds scripts/generate-schema, so a\nretired pair was PUBLISHED to JSON consumers in docs/schema.json. This defect class can\nescape the docstring layer into a shipped artifact.\n\nCURRENT STATE (2026-09-30): those nine sites were cleaned by hand (PRs #414/#416). Every\nremaining hit for those names under packages/*/src is fold-explanation prose (e.g.\ncompact.py:27/137, route_handler.py:5, axis_meta_keys.py:423 \"folded from\",\nrouter_routes.py:25, controller_routes.py:51, message_queue.py:6). The CLASS is still\nunguarded: nothing would catch the next one. The docstring-staleness-audit playbook records\nthe blind spot and a manual grep stopgap until this check lands.\n\nPROPOSED CHECK (a fourth sub-check in scripts/check-docstring-drift). For every .py under\npackages/*/src/, extract the module docstring and inline comments, and report each\nidentifier-shaped token (snake_case, or a kind=\"...\" literal) that looks like vocabulary but\nis in NONE of the live registries. Report it with file:line and the token. The comparison set\nmust be built from the resolvers:\n  - edge_types.all_edge_type_names()   (NOT edge_types.EDGE_TYPES, which is a tuple of\n    EdgeTypeSpec objects, so `name in EDGE_TYPES` is always False)\n  - symbol_kinds.all_symbol_kind_names()\n  - evidence_types.all_evidence_type_names(). Required: message_send is a LIVE evidence\n    type (evidence_types.py:312) as well as a retired edge-type name, and prose such as\n    websocket.py:161 uses it correctly. An edge + symbol-kind-only set would flag it.\n    Consider the io-boundary vocabulary too.\n\nWHY THIS SHAPE IS SAFE, unlike the sweep-skipper #410 refuted. It is name-EXACT and\nregistry-derived: no blame heuristic, no date arithmetic and no threshold, so it cannot decay\nwith the calendar the way the day-delta arm did (28 -> 87 flags with nothing drifted). The\nregistries are already the single source of truth and are CI-enforced for drift\n(check-edge-type-drift, check-symbol-kind-drift, check-evidence-type-drift). This extends the\nsame authority to prose.\n\nKNOWN FALSE-POSITIVE SOURCE, and the answer. Docstrings legitimately name retired types while\nEXPLAINING the fold; those must not flag. Cheapest first: (a) suppress a hit whose line also\nmatches /fold|retired|pre-fold|deprecated|was .* onto|no longer/; (b) require an explicit\nallowlist comment. The fold-explanation sites listed under CURRENT STATE are the test set for\n(a). MEASURE the FP rate on the live tree before wiring it as a gate.\n\nDO NOT wire this as a blocking gate on the first pass. Land it as a reported sub-check under\n--all, measure, then decide.\n\nRevised 2026-09-30 from the premise check (see discussion)."  # 4592
- op: discuss  # 2b5f
  at: '2026-10-02T00:59:27Z'  # 2b5f
  by: agent  # 2b5f
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 2b5f
  clock: 6  # 2b5f
  nonce: 2b5f  # 2b5f
  message: "IMPLEMENTED (concurrent run 2026-10-01, unmerged): local branch jgstern-agent/feat/sipuk-registry-refs, commits fcd4d7afd3 + 514e1495e8, on origin/dev 96155dd17f. No push or PR; integration is downstream.\n\nWHAT: scripts/check-docstring-drift gains a fourth sub-check, --registry-refs, which is also included in --all. It is reported only and never changes the exit code. It masks each .py file down to its prose: comments, plus string literals containing whitespace (docstrings at any level, MetaKeySpec-style descriptions). In that prose it finds names presented as vocabulary (\"X edges\", \"edge type is X\", kind=\"X\", evidence_type=\"X\") and reports each one that is in none of the live registries. Those are the edge types, symbol kinds, evidence types, meta keys and io-boundary kinds, all read via their all_*_names() resolvers. A hit whose sentence explains a fold is listed as fold_explained, not flagged. Files it cannot tokenize are listed as NOT SCANNED. The playbook's \"Until WI-sipuk lands\" stopgap now documents the sub-check and its measured limits.\n\nMEASURED. Pre-fold tree 22418804f4^, against the 63 retired-name lines that commit removed: 18/19 files and 36/63 lines flagged, and 0/63 suppressed as fold explanations. The missed file is markdown.py, a definition list. The missed lines are arrow bullets in files that do flag. Live tree, via the shipped CLI: 368 files, 16 flagged, 24 fold_explained, 0 unscanned, exit 0. Of the 16:\n- 7 are real retired-vocabulary drift (renders x3, enqueues x2, crdt_publishes x2), filed as WI-ridan.\n- 4 are a real code/registry disagreement: lua_ffi and napi emit evidence types the registry lacks. The docstrings are right. Filed as WI-pubin (P2).\n- 5 are false positives.\nI read all 24 fold_explained hits; each is a genuine fold explanation. The item's own correction (evidence types in the comparison set) is applied as the item states it, as a union over the registries. Measured cost: 1 of the 63 lines, 0 files.\n\nTESTS: 25 new tests in tests/test_check_docstring_drift.py. RED against the origin/dev script: 18 failed / 13 passed (that run had 18 of the new tests; the rest came later). GREEN: targeted smart-test, 12 files, 208 passed, 0 failed, mypy ratchet clean. Each mutation of a pinned rule (union, guards, anchored list, history words, whitespace rule, barrier, de-dup) turns its fixture red; probed ad hoc.\n\nNOT DONE: the tracker-refs \"adjacent token\" refinement from discussion 1 is a different sub-check and is untouched. NOT MEASURED: precision on any repository but this one; the 130 pre-fold-tree hits outside the 63 were not adjudicated. Gating is NOT proposed: 5/16 false positives on the live tree is too many for a gate."  # 2b5f
